  description: Pluto is a dwarf planet located in the Kuiper Belt, a region of icy
    objects beyond Neptune. It has a complex surface featuring frozen nitrogen, mountains
    of water ice, and bright plains, along with five known moons.
  interestingFact: Pluto's largest moon, Charon, is so large compared with Pluto
    that their shared center of orbit lies outside Pluto itself.
